        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/create-sticky-note.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "4. Decide where it goes — `todos/` is the default, not the only answer",
      "prov:value": "| destination | when | what it becomes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`todos/items/`** — the default | somebody has an outstanding item | a `todo/1.0.0` node: `status`, `priority`, `origin`, plus the tags below |\n| **`todos/feedback/`** | it is about a specific block, with the submitter's identity | the content-review feedback workflow the `todo-review` skill reads |\n| **`folio/`** | it belongs on a rendered page | a landing sticky — but a *page's* sticky is a layer's **contribution**, so it is declared in that layer's `<name>.json`, not written here. A landing sticky lives in the `folio/` of **the instance it describes**, never in another instance's (bean `1yd7`), so a mounted instance's sticky arrives with the mount. `cat-harness/folio/` still holds other instances' stickies until `1yd7` moves them — do not add one there |\n| **nowhere** | it was worth showing and not worth keeping | previewed in the conversation and left there |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 1yd7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/create-sticky-note.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "6. Preview, on the surface the reader is on",
      "prov:value": "**On the knowledge graph** when the note is one of many, or when its look\nmatters — build the page and screenshot it. A rendered artefact cannot be\nassessed from a description of it, and this repository has the measurement:\nthree defects in the sticky board were invisible to a green suite and visible\nthe moment somebody looked."
    }
  ]
